## Research & References

- **THC in Breath Aerosols – NCBI/PMC** — [Link](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC10201171/) 
— Supports investigation of **THC detection in exhaled-breath aerosols**.

- **Cannabinoids in Exhaled Breath Condensate – NCBI/PMC** — [Link](https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC11264354/)
— Supports **breath condensation for cannabinoid recovery**.

- **THC Detection in Exhaled Breath – Forensic Toxicology** — [Link](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11419-016-0333-x)
— Supports the **feasibility of THC detection in exhaled breath**.

- **Electrochemical THC Detection Review** — [Link](https://jcannabisresearch.biomedcentral.com/articles/10.1186/s42238-022-00122-3)
— Supports **electrochemical sensing approaches for THC detection**.

- **Ott et al. – Fentanyl Detection Using SPCE** — [DOI](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jelechem.2020.114425) 
— Supports **SPCE-based voltammetric fentanyl detection**.

- **Jordan & Hart – Morphine Voltammetry** — [Link](https://pubs.rsc.org/en/content/articlelanding/1991/an/an9911600991) 
— Supports the **electrochemical basis for morphine detection**.

- **Karlovits et al. – Open-Source Potentiostat** — [PDF](https://bioresources.cnr.ncsu.edu/wp-content/uploads/2021/04/BioRes_16_2_3916_Karlovits_KTR_Cyclic_Voltammetry_Paper_Printed_Electrode_Potentiostat_18442.pdf) 
— Supports **open-source potentiostat and SPCE measurements**.

- **Rodeostat – Open-Source Potentiostat** — [OSHWA](https://certification.oshwa.org/us002129.html) 
— Supports the **open-hardware potentiostat platform used in our prototype**.

- **Setiawan & Lelono – Electronic Nose** — [Link](https://etd.repository.ugm.ac.id/penelitian/detail/150890) 
— Supports **VOC-array pattern sensing for electronic-nose classification**.

